Source: sauron
Section: web
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Kefah Issa <kefah@oodi.iq>
# No cargo/nodejs here on purpose. packaging/deb/build-deb.sh owns compilation and
# debian/rules never invokes a compiler (every dh_auto_* is overridden to a no-op),
# exactly as packaging/rpm/build-rpm.sh --prebuilt does for the RPM path. Adding a
# toolchain here would not make `dh` build anything; it would only slow the
# package job down and make the two formats diverge.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/edraj/sauron
# Nothing is chowned at build time — see debian/sauron-server.postinst for why
# ownership is applied at configure time instead — so the build needs no fakeroot.
Rules-Requires-Root: no

# Every binary package is Architecture: any, including the two that hold no ELF
# (sauron and sauron-dashboard). Marking those `all` would be more correct, but it
# forces the arch:any -> arch:all dependencies to use `(= ${source:Version})`
# instead of `(= ${binary:Version})`, and getting that wrong produces packages
# that simply cannot be co-installed. The RPM makes all four subpackages
# arch-specific too. Uniform `any` keeps one dependency idiom across the set;
# revisit only if these are ever published to a real multi-arch archive.

Package: sauron
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: Unified error reporting and product analytics platform (common files)
 Sauron collects crashes, errors and product analytics from applications through
 SDKs, and serves them through a web dashboard.
 .
 This package holds the pieces every other sauron package needs: the shared
 /etc/sauron configuration directory, the service account definition and the
 state directories under /var/lib/sauron.

Package: sauron-server
Architecture: any
Depends: sauron (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
# postgresql and redis-server are Recommends, not Depends: both are routinely run
# on a different host from the one Sauron is installed on, so hard-requiring them
# would drag a local database onto every deployment that already has one.
# The RPM says `Recommends: valkey`; neither Debian 12 nor Ubuntu 22.04 ships a
# valkey package, so the Debian-family equivalent is redis-server.
Recommends: postgresql, redis-server
Description: Sauron backend services (API, ingest, monitor, tier, migrate)
 The long-running Sauron daemons, their systemd units and per-service
 configuration:
 .
  * sauron-api       - dashboard API
  * sauron-ingest    - SDK ingest edge and worker pool
  * sauron-monitor   - uptime prober
  * sauron-alerts    - alert rule evaluator
  * sauron-tier      - hot/cold Parquet tiering
  * sauron-storesync - app store metrics syncer
  * sauron-inspector - PII inspector (opt-in, not enabled on install)
  * sauron-migrate   - one-shot schema migrator
 .
 Postgres and Redis are treated as external services; see
 /usr/share/doc/sauron-server/SETUP.md.

Package: sauron-dashboard
Architecture: any
Depends: sauron (= ${binary:Version}), nginx, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Sauron web dashboard (static SPA served by nginx)
 The Sauron single-page dashboard, served as static files by the system nginx
 through a drop-in at /etc/nginx/conf.d/sauron-dashboard.conf.
 .
 The browser-facing API URLs are runtime configuration, not build-time: edit
 /etc/sauron/dashboard.env and run /usr/libexec/sauron/sauron-dashboard-config
 to regenerate config.js, then reload nginx.

Package: sauron-cli
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Sauron command-line tools
 Standalone Sauron command-line tools, installable without the server:
 .
  * crebain       - load and benchmark generator
  * sauron-symcli - symbolication CLI
